  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Climate and Disaster Resilience in Nepal (CDRIN)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of CDRIN is to build more resilient local economies and communities that can withstand the impact of climate change, promote sustainable development and contribute to the achievement of the Paris Agreement and localisation of the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).

CDRIN end-of-program outcomes (EOPO) are: 
EOPO 1: Reduced risk of landslide hazards to minimise loss of lives and damage of properties in Nepal  
EOPO 2: Increased local government&#x2019;s access to climate finance to implement climate change mitigation and adaptation investments in Nepal (UNCDF)
EOPO 3: A standard and internationally recognised mechanism of performance-based climate resilience grants established and institutionalised in Nepal (UNCDF)</narrative>
  </description>
